{
  "name": "BytesKnowItsMime",
  "comment": "Stage 1 (decision 867): a type is born whole — the registered type hands itself to the\nvalue. An image read from bytes carries the REGISTERED image.kind.png (from its\n`[Format(\"png\", \"image/png\", Compressible = false)]` attribute); its mime is the kind's\nmime, not the image's own `_mime` copy. Red on runtime2: today `type.@this(...)` at\n`type/this.cs:149` makes a fresh `kind.@this(\"png\")` from the name alone — a bare kind\nwhose `_mime` field defaults to `[]`, so `%img!type.kind.mime[0]%` reads null. Fixture\nphoto.png committed alongside (copied from test/app/type/kind/strict/).",
  "step": [
